# Keeps the build context to exactly what the image needs to run. Without
# this, `docker build` sends every file under ./backend to the daemon and
# COPY . . bakes all of it into the image layer — including host-side
# artifacts from local test runs (__pycache__, .pytest_cache), which then
# ship in the production image owned by whatever user ran the test, not
# appuser. Found and cleaned 2026-08-20 (docs/SELF_HOSTING.md).
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/
htmlcov/
.coverage
.env
.env.*
*.log
.git/
.gitignore
